.SS "int32_t schultz_panel_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a panel: a background, a border and a corner radius\&. The plainest widget there is, and the one every container is built from\&. It paints \fCbackground\fP, then strokes \fCborder\&.color\fP at \fCborder\&.width\fP, both rounded by \fCcorner\&.radius\fP\&. A fully transparent background paints nothing, which is the default, so a panel is invisible until it is styled\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a label: static text drawn in \fCtext\&.color\fP\&. The text is copied\&. Measuring shapes it against the width it is offered, so a label's height depends on its width, which is the case the whole text pipeline and the measure signature were built around\&. Wrapping is on by default\&.
.PP
A label needs the tree's font system, set with schultz_tree_set_font_system\&. Without one it measures to nothing and draws nothing rather than guessing at a font\&.
.PP
The font comes from the resolved \fCfont\fP property\&. Note that a loaded font is bound to a pixel size, so \fCfont\&.size\fP is currently advisory: it does not re-load the face\&. That is a known seam\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The text, NUL terminated and copied\&. NULL means empty\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_set_spans (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const \fBschultz_span\fP * spans, uint32_t count)"

.PP
Says which stretches of a label's text are not set the way its style says\&. A bold phrase inside a sentence, a term in the code face, a word with a background or a line through it\&. Anything no span covers is drawn the way it was before, so a plain label needs none of this\&.
.PP
The list is copied, link strings and all, so the caller may free or reuse whatever it built them from\&. Spans covering nothing, or bytes past the end of the text, are dropped\&.
.PP
Setting the text clears the spans, because a span is byte offsets into the words that were there and means nothing once they change\&. Set the text first, then the spans\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.br
\fIspans\fP The spans\&. May be NULL when count is zero\&. 
.br
\fIcount\fP How many spans\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a label, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for NULL spans with a nonzero count, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const \fBschultz_span\fP * schultz_label_spans (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint32_t * out_count)"

