.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_set_ellipsize (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t ellipsize)"

.PP
Turns a label's ellipsis on or off\&. Off, which is how a label starts, a line too long for the box it is given is drawn anyway and runs past the edge, over whatever is beside it\&.
.PP
On, the line is cut where it stops fitting and the cut is marked with an ellipsis, so the reader can see that there is more\&. Nothing is drawn outside the box either way, and a box too narrow even for the ellipsis draws nothing at all\&.
.PP
This is what a caption, a table cell or a list row wants: the text is whatever the application put there, and the width is whatever the layout had left\&. A paragraph wants wrapping instead\&.
.PP
A label still asks for the width its whole text needs, so turning this on never makes a label narrower\&. It only decides what happens when the layout cannot give it that width\&.
.PP
Right to left text is not cut, because its end is the start of the string\&. It is held inside the box by clipping alone\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.br
\fIellipsize\fP Nonzero to cut and mark, zero to let the text overflow\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a label\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_set_selectable (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t selectable)"

.PP
Lets a label's text be selected and copied\&. Off by default, because turning it on everywhere would change what a click on a caption does\&. A form's labels are not meant to be dragged across; a paragraph of prose is\&.
.PP
A selectable label is still not focusable, so it does not join the tab order\&. Copy reaches it through the tree's selection owner instead; see schultz_tree_set_selection_owner\&.
.PP
With a mouse, a press places one end and a drag moves the other, a double click takes a word and a triple click takes the whole text\&. With a finger, a press held still for a moment takes the word under it and puts a grip on each end to move them with, so that an ordinary drag is left free to mean scroll\&.
.PP
Control with C copies the selection and control with A takes all of it\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.br
\fIselectable\fP Nonzero to allow selection, zero to disallow it and drop whatever was selected\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a label\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_selectable (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Reports whether a label's text can be selected\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 when the text can be selected, 0 otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_set_selection (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint32_t start, uint32_t end)"

.PP
Selects part of a label's text\&. Offsets are in bytes into the label's UTF-8 text, and are clamped to its length\&. Passing the same value twice selects nothing\&. Selecting anything takes the tree's selection away from whatever held it\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.br
\fIstart\fP One end of the selection, in bytes\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP The other end, in bytes\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a label, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when it is not selectable\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_selection (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint32_t * out_start, uint32_t * out_end)"

.PP
Reports what part of a label's text is selected\&. The two offsets come back in order however the selection was made, so start is never greater than end\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.br
\fIout_start\fP Receives the first selected byte\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIout_end\fP Receives one past the last\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a NULL output or a node that is not a label, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_label_copy_selection (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Puts a label's selected text on the clipboard\&. What control with C does, exposed so that a menu item can do it too\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_label_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a label, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when nothing is selected\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_separator_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, uint32_t orientation, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a separator: a single rule in \fCborder\&.color\fP\&. Measures thin on its own axis and to nothing on the other, so a horizontal separator in a VBox takes a line's worth of height and the full width\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIorientation\fP SCHULTZ_ORIENT_HORIZONTAL or _VERTICAL\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_ellipse_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates an ellipse filling the node's bounds\&. Fills with \fCbackground\fP and strokes with \fCborder\&.color\fP at \fCborder\&.width\fP\&. A square node gives a circle; there is no separate circle widget because there is no separate behaviour\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_line_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_point\fP from, \fBschultz_point\fP to, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a line between two points inside the node's bounds\&. The points are in the node's own space, so they move with it\&. Strokes with \fCborder\&.color\fP at \fCborder\&.width\fP\&.
