.SS "int32_t schultz_button_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a button: a box with a centred caption\&. The caption is a Label child, so it is styled and measured like any other text\&. The button sizes itself around it, with padding from the resolved \fCpadding\fP property\&.
.PP
A click reaches the host; the button does not consume it, because pressing a button is exactly the thing the host wants to hear about\&. Space and enter activate it, which the router does for any node declaring SCHULTZ_ACTION_CLICK\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. NULL means empty\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_button_label (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Returns a button's caption node\&. Use it to change the caption with schultz_label_set_text, or to style the text on its own\&.
.PP
Every button in the toolkit answers, not only a plain one: a toggle button, a menu button and a split menu button are all made as buttons and keep the caption a button is made with\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. NULL yields SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A button, made by schultz_button_create, schultz_toggle_button_create, schultz_menu_button_create or schultz_split_menu_button_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The Label child, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE when the node is not one of those\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_hyperlink_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a hyperlink: a button drawn as a link\&. Text in the accent colour with no border or background, underlined while the pointer is over it, and focusable and keyboard activated like any other button\&.
.PP
The toolkit opens nothing\&. The click reaches the host through the event queue with the node's token, and what the link points at is the host's business\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_hyperlink_set_text (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const char * text)"

.PP
Replaces a hyperlink's caption\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_hyperlink_create\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The new caption, copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_hyperlink_set_visited (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t visited)"

.PP
Marks a link as followed, which draws it in the muted colour\&. Only the host knows whether the target was reached, so only the host can set this\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
