.SS "int32_t schultz_toggle_button_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, uint32_t group, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a toggle button: a button that stays pressed\&. Drawn as a button and selected rather than checked, since the selected state is what the toolkit paints in the accent everywhere else\&.
.PP
A group number works the way schultz_radio_create's does: only equality matters, and a group is the siblings sharing a parent and that number\&. Selecting one clears the rest, which is what makes a row of them a segmented control\&. \fBGroup 0 means ungrouped\fP, and an ungrouped toggle button turns on and off freely\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. 
.br
\fIgroup\fP Group number, or 0 for ungrouped\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_toggle_button_select (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Selects a toggle button, clearing the rest of its group\&. An ungrouped button flips instead, since it has no group to be exclusive within\&. A grouped button that is already selected does not turn off, the way a radio does not\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_toggle_button_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_toggle_button_is_selected (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Reports whether a toggle button is on\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_toggle_button_create\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 when selected, 0 otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_button_bar_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a button bar: a row ordered by convention, not by insertion\&. A host adds its buttons in whatever order suits its code and each one says what it is for\&. The bar puts them where the platform expects, so the same dialog has Cancel on the correct side everywhere\&.
.PP
Buttons sit against the right edge, except one given SCHULTZ_BUTTON_ROLE_LEFT, which is pinned to the left and left out of the ordering\&. Every button is sized to the widest unless that is turned off\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_button_bar_add (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const char * text, uint32_t role, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_button)"

.PP
Adds a button to a bar\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the bar\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_button_bar_create\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. 
.br
\fIrole\fP One of the SCHULTZ_BUTTON_ROLE_* values\&. 
.br
\fIout_button\fP Receives the new button, or NULL if it is not wanted\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_button_bar_set_role (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP button, uint32_t role)"

.PP
Says what an existing node in a bar is for\&. This is how anything other than a plain button joins a bar: add it as a child of the bar and then give it a role\&.
