.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_checkbox_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a checkbox: a tick box with a caption beside it\&. Clicking it flips SCHULTZ_STATE_CHECKED on itself, and the click still reaches the host so it can act on the new value\&. The box is a square of the row height; its fill is \fCbackground\fP, its outline \fCborder\&.color\fP, and the tick \fCselection\&.color\fP, all of which change with the checked state through the state patches the constructor installs\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. NULL or empty means no caption\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_switch_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a switch: a checkbox that draws as a sliding track\&. Identical to a checkbox in every way but its painting, which is what a switch is: the same two state choice, shown as on or off rather than as ticked or not\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. NULL or empty means no caption\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_radio_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, const char * text, uint32_t group, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a radio button, one of a mutually exclusive set\&. A group is the radios that share a parent and a group number, so two groups on one screen need no coordination beyond sitting in different containers\&. Clicking one selects it and clears the rest of its group; unlike a checkbox, clicking the selected one changes nothing, because one of a set is always chosen\&.
.PP
Because the group is the parent, a radio taken out of the tree with schultz_node_set_parent is in no group: selecting it clears nothing, and nothing clears it\&. It keeps whatever it was set to, and putting it back joins it to the group again for the next click but does not settle the group as it stands\&. So a radio removed while selected comes back selected beside whichever one was chosen in its absence, and both read as chosen until one of them is clicked\&. Call schultz_radio_select on the one that should win after putting it back\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP The caption, copied\&. NULL or empty means no caption\&. 
.br
\fIgroup\fP Group number\&. Any value; only equality matters\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

