.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_canvas_fill_path (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const uint8_t * steps, uint32_t step_count, const \fBschultz_point\fP * points, uint32_t point_count, \fBschultz_paint\fP paint, uint32_t rule)"

.PP
Records a filled path, which may curve and may have holes\&. The counterpart to schultz_canvas_fill_polygon for anything straight sides cannot say\&. The two arrays are read together: each step takes the points it needs off the front of the second, so their counts differ and both are given\&. See SCHULTZ_PATH_MOVE and the values beside it\&.
.PP
Both arrays are copied\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A canvas that is recording\&. 
.br
\fIsteps\fP SCHULTZ_PATH_* values, beginning with a move\&. 
.br
\fIstep_count\fP How many steps\&. 
.br
\fIpoints\fP The points the steps use\&. 
.br
\fIpoint_count\fP How many points the steps together ask for\&. 
.br
\fIpaint\fP What to fill with\&. 
.br
\fIrule\fP SCHULTZ_FILL_NONZERO or SCHULTZ_FILL_EVEN_ODD\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_canvas_stroke_path (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const uint8_t * steps, uint32_t step_count, const \fBschultz_point\fP * points, uint32_t point_count, \fBschultz_stroke\fP stroke)"

.PP
Records a stroked path, which may curve and may have holes\&. A subpath that ends in a close is stroked all the way round; one that does not stops at its last point, wearing the stroke's cap at each end\&. That is the difference between an outline and an open curve, and it is said in the path rather than in a separate argument\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A canvas that is recording\&. 
.br
\fIsteps\fP SCHULTZ_PATH_* values, beginning with a move\&. 
.br
\fIstep_count\fP How many steps\&. 
.br
\fIpoints\fP The points the steps use\&. 
.br
\fIpoint_count\fP How many points the steps together ask for\&. 
.br
\fIstroke\fP What the outline is drawn with\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_canvas_text (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, const char * utf8, float x, float y, \fBschultz_paint\fP paint)"

.PP
Records text, shaped once and replayed thereafter\&. The position is the leading edge of the baseline, which is what the text pipeline works in\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL, and must have a font system\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A canvas that is recording\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A loaded font\&. 
.br
\fIutf8\fP The text, NUL terminated\&. 
.br
\fIx\fP Where the text starts\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP The baseline\&. 
.br
\fIpaint\fP What to draw the letters with\&. A gradient is measured across the run's own bounds, so it reads the same whatever the words are\&. An emoji keeps its own colours and ignores a gradient\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when there is no font system, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_canvas_stroke_text (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_handle\fP font, const char * utf8, float x, float y, \fBschultz_stroke\fP stroke)"

.PP
Records text drawn as an outline rather than filled in\&. The letters are taken from the font's own outlines and stroked, so this is a heading with a rule round it rather than a heading\&. It costs more than schultz_canvas_text, which draws from pictures of each letter the toolkit keeps, so it is for the few words that want it rather than for prose\&.
.PP
A glyph that is a picture rather than an outline, such as an emoji, cannot be stroked and is left out\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL, and must have a font system\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A canvas that is recording\&. 
.br
\fIfont\fP A loaded font\&. 
.br
\fIutf8\fP The text, NUL terminated\&. 
.br
\fIx\fP Where the text starts\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP The baseline\&. 
.br
\fIstroke\fP What the outline is drawn with\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when there is no font system, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint32_t schultz_canvas_count (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

