\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the accordion\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_accordion_create\&. 
.br
\fIheader\fP The section's header node\&. 
.br
\fIexpanded\fP Nonzero to open it\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_accordion_is_expanded (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP header)"

.PP
Reports whether a section is open\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the section\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fIheader\fP The section's header node\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 when open, 0 otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_accordion_set_single_expand (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t on)"

.PP
Chooses whether more than one section may be open\&. Off by default\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the accordion\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_accordion_create\&. 
.br
\fIon\fP Nonzero to allow only one open at a time\&. 
.RE
