.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, int32_t captures, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a popup: a panel that floats over the page, anchored to a node\&. This is the plain one, and the thing the others are made of\&. It looks like a panel a step above the page, with square corners and no triangle, which is what a dropdown or a menu wants\&. The date, time and colour pickers all open one\&.
.PP
A popover and a tooltip are popups too, made by the two calls below\&. They differ only in how they are dressed; everything after they are made is done with the popup calls, because they are popups\&. There is one set of verbs here and several ways to start\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIcaptures\fP Nonzero to close on a press outside and swallow it, which is what a chooser wants; zero to let presses through\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popover_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, int32_t captures, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a popover: a popup that points at what it belongs to\&. A bubble rather than a panel\&. It carries a triangle aimed at the node it was opened against, sits centred on that node, and is drawn in the colours opposite the page so that it reads as being in front of the page rather than part of it\&.
.PP
Drive it with the popup calls: schultz_popup_open, _close, _content and the rest all take one of these, because one of these is a popup\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIcaptures\fP Nonzero to close on a press outside and swallow it; zero to let presses through\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_tooltip_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, const char * text, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a tooltip: a small non capturing panel holding one line\&. Show and hide it yourself with schultz_popup_open and _close, or hand it a node to watch with schultz_tooltip_watch and let it decide\&.
.PP
It is invisible to the pointer throughout, since it sits over the thing it explains and one that took a click would make that thing unclickable\&. A panel that can be clicked is a popover\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP What it says, copied\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_tooltip_watch (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_handle\fP anchor, uint32_t delay_ms)"

.PP
Has a tooltip watch a node and show itself when the pointer rests\&. The tooltip appears once the pointer has been over the node for the delay, and goes away as soon as it leaves\&. It reads the hover flag the router already keeps, so watching costs nothing at the routing layer, and it needs the tree's clock: a host that never calls schultz_tree_advance will never see it appear\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding both\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A tooltip, or any popover\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP The node to watch, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE to stop watching\&. 
.br
\fIdelay_ms\fP How long the pointer must rest before it shows\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a popover, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_popup_content (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Returns the node an application fills with a popover's contents\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. NULL yields SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A popover or tooltip node\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The content node, or SCHULTZ_HANDLE_NONE when the node is neither\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_set_arrow (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t arrow)"

.PP
Turns a popover's little triangle on or off\&. On for a popover, because a bubble that points at what it belongs to is how a reader knows which control it is about\&. Off for a plain panel dropped under a control, such as the calendar a date picker opens, where the panel is plainly the field's and an arrow only adds noise\&.
.PP
The triangle lives inside the popover's own bounds, on whichever side it ends up on, so the content sits clear of it and nothing has to be told to repaint a wider area\&.
.PP
It also decides how the popover lines up\&. A bubble is centred on what it points at, because the triangle has to come out of the middle of it; a panel with no triangle lines up with the leading edge of the control, the way a dropdown does\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_popup_create\&. 
.br
\fIarrow\fP Nonzero to draw one, zero for a plain box\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_set_gap (float gap)"

.PP
How far a popover or a tooltip sits from what it belongs to\&. Four by default\&. One setting for the whole toolkit rather than one per node, the way the toast's edge is, because it is a clearance rather than a decision about one widget\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIgap\fP The clearance\&. Zero sits flush; negative is refused\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_open (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_handle\fP anchor)"

.PP
Shows a popover beside something, where it belongs\&. Above what it was opened against and centred on it, with a little clearance and its triangle pointing back down at it\&. That way the control being talked about stays under the reader's eye instead of being covered by the bubble talking about it\&.
.PP
A tooltip goes below instead, out of the way of the pointer resting on the widget, and lines up with the pointer rather than with the widget's corner\&.
.PP
Either flips to the other side sooner than be cut off by the edge of the window, and only then: a popover with room above it is always above\&.
.PP
Use schultz_popup_open_at to name a side yourself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding both\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_popup_create\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP What it belongs to\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_open_at (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_handle\fP anchor, uint32_t placement)"

.PP
Shows a popover on a side you name\&. For a panel that belongs somewhere in particular whatever the toolkit would have chosen: the calendar a date picker drops under its field is below, because that is where a dropdown goes\&.
.PP
It still moves aside rather than off the screen, and still flips when the side named does not fit and the other one does\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding both\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_popup_create\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP What it belongs to\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIplacement\fP One of SCHULTZ_PLACE_*\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_close (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Closes a popover or tooltip\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A popover or tooltip node\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_popup_is_open (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Reports whether a popover or tooltip is showing\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A popover or tooltip node\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 when open, 0 otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_dialog_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, const char * title, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a dialog: a titled panel over a scrim covering the window\&. The scrim dims what is behind and swallows every press that misses the panel, which is what modal means\&. A press beside the panel does not close it: a dialog is asking a question, and clicking elsewhere is not an answer\&. Escape does close it\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItitle\fP The heading, copied\&. NULL means none\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or an error as above\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_dialog_content (const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node)"

.PP
Returns the node an application fills with a dialog's contents\&. 
.PP
