.SS "int32_t schultz_message_dialog_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, const char * title, uint32_t icon, uint32_t buttons, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a message dialog: an icon, a message, and standard buttons\&. Built on schultz_dialog_create, so it hangs off the root and dims what is behind it\&. The buttons are laid out by a button bar, so they sit where the platform expects\&.
.PP
Enter answers with OK and Escape with Cancel, or with OK when OK is the only button there is\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItitle\fP The dialog's title, copied\&. 
.br
\fIicon\fP One of the SCHULTZ_DIALOG_ICON_* values\&. 
.br
\fIbuttons\fP One of the SCHULTZ_DIALOG_* button set values\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_message_dialog_set_text (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, const char * message, const char * detail)"

.PP
Sets the message and the smaller line under it\&. An empty or NULL detail takes no room rather than leaving a blank line\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the dialog\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by any of the three dialog calls\&. 
