.SS "int32_t schultz_toast_show (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, const char * text, uint32_t ms, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Shows a brief message that takes itself away again\&. The toast hangs off the root, sits centred against whichever edge was chosen, and never takes the pointer or the keyboard\&. Several showing at once stack rather than overlapping\&.
.PP
The countdown runs on the tree's clock, so a host that stops drawing frames stops the toast going away with it\&.
.PP
A toast whose time is up is hidden rather than destroyed, and the next call reuses it, so showing a hundred toasts does not build a hundred nodes\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to show it in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItext\fP What it says, copied\&. 
.br
\fIms\fP How long to show it\&. Must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the toast, or NULL if it is not wanted\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

