.SS "int32_t schultz_tree_view_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a tree view: a list view whose rows hold rows\&. The hierarchy is the node tree rather than a model beside it\&. A row is a header and a column of child rows; collapsing hides the column, and indentation comes from depth\&. A row with no children draws no triangle\&.
.PP
Rows are named by handle rather than by position, because a row's position changes whenever anything above it opens or closes\&.
.PP
The up and down keys walk the rows a reader can see, skipping what is closed\&. Right opens a closed row and steps into an open one; left closes an open row and steps out of a closed one\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_tree_view_add (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent_row, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_row)"

.PP
Adds a row and returns the node to fill\&. Rows start closed\&. The returned node is what every other tree view call takes back\&.
.PP
