.SS "int32_t schultz_number_field_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, double minimum, double maximum, double value, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a number field: a text field with a down and an up button\&. The two steps sit to the right of the field, down then up, and each is a square as tall as the row rather than half of one, so a finger can aim at either\&. That makes the whole thing about twice as wide as the field alone\&.
.PP
Typing is read when the field is left or when Enter is pressed, so a half typed number is not fought with while it is being typed\&. Text that is not a number puts the last good value back rather than guessing\&.
.PP
Holding a step button repeats it after a short pause, so one press is one step\&. The up and down arrow keys step it too\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIminimum\fP Lowest value it will take\&. 
.br
\fImaximum\fP Highest value\&. Must not be below the minimum\&. 
.br
\fIvalue\fP Where to start\&. Clamped into the range\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_number_field_set_steps (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint32_t where)"

.PP
Moves the two step buttons beside the field or above and below it\&. Beside is the default and is what a number on its own wants\&. Above and below is for several of them side by side, where three fields each twice their own width will not fit: it trades the width for height and keeps the buttons big enough to aim at\&. The time picker's popup uses it\&.
.PP
A preferred width set on the number field means the whole widget, so the same number is a much wider field above and below than it is beside\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_number_field_create\&. 
.br
\fIwhere\fP SCHULTZ_STEPS_BESIDE or SCHULTZ_STEPS_ABOVE_BELOW\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for anything else\&. 
.RE
.PP

