.SS "int32_t schultz_lottie_create (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP parent, \fBschultz_handle\fP image, \fBschultz_handle\fP * out_node)"

.PP
Creates a view that plays a Lottie animation\&. It measures to the animation's natural size, which a size hint overrules, and draws whichever frame the animation is on, stretched to the node\&. The artwork is vector, so it is drawn at that size rather than resampled to it\&.
.PP
It starts paused on the first frame and loops once played\&. Playing is what asks the tree's clock to tick it, so a paused view costs nothing, and a host that never calls schultz_tree_advance will see it sit still\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree to create in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP The parent node\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIimage\fP A handle from schultz_image_load_animation\&. 
.br
\fIout_node\fP Receives the new node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_lottie_play (\fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, int32_t playing)"

.PP
Starts or stops an animation\&. Frames advance by however long has passed rather than one per tick, so playback runs at the speed it was authored at whatever rate the host draws\&. A view that reaches the end without looping stops itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItree\fP The tree holding the node\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP A node created by schultz_lottie_create\&. 
.br
\fIplaying\fP Nonzero to run\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE when the node is not a Lottie view, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

